  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-303(a)): EXCEPT AS PROVIDED IN SUBSECTION (B) OF THIS SECTION, A person shall have a permit issued under this subtitle before the person carries, wears, or transports a handgun.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-303(b)): A PERSON WHO HAS THE WRITTEN CONSENT OF THE GOVERNING BOARD OF A BONA FIDE CHURCH TO CARRY A HANDGUN ON THE PROPERTY OF THE CHURCH DURING SERVICES AND GATHERINGS, AND WHO HAS THE INTENT TO CARRY, WEAR, OR TRANSPORT A HANDGUN FOR PURPOSES RELATED TO SELF–PROTECTION OR THE PROTECTION OF OTHERS WHILE ON THE PROPERTY OF THE CHURCH MAY, WITHOUT A PERMIT, WITH ADVANCE NOTICE TO THE PRIMARY LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY OF THE COUNTY: (1) CARRY A HANDGUN ON THE PROPERTY OF THE CHURCH DURING SERVICES AND GATHERINGS; AND (2) TRANSPORT A HANDGUN TO AND FROM SERVICES AND GATHERINGS OF THE CHURCH."
